{"strongs": "H0954", "word": "בּוֺשׁ", "translit": "bush", "root": "בוש", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be ashamed", "definition": "בּוֺשׁ 109 verb be ashamed (Sabean בוס ; מהבאס = evil-doer DHM ZMG 1883, 375, || Aramaic בְּהַת , Syriac ; Arabic , mean disperse ) — Qal Perfect Jer 48:39 בּשׁ Jer 48:13 בּוֺשָׁה Jer 15:9 בּשְׁתִּי Jer 31:19 + 25 t.; Imperfect יֵבוֺשׁ Isa 29:22 + 57 t.; Infinitive absolute בּוֺשׁ Jer 6:15 ; Jer 8:12 Imperative בּוֺשִׁי Isa 23:4 ; Ezek 16:52 , בּוֺשׁוּ Ezek 36:32 Participle plural בּוֺשִׁים Ezek 32:30 — 1. absolute feel shame Jer 6:15 + 16 t., Isa 19:9 ; Isa 23:4 ; Isa 37:27 Isa 2 , Isa 45:16 + 14 t., Ezek 16:63 ; Mic 7:16 ; Joel 2:26 ; Joel 2:27 ; 2Kgs 19:26 ; Ezek 9:6 ; Job 6:20 ; Ps 6:11 (+ 27 t., chiefly in late Psalms). 2. followed by מִן , be ashamed of , i.e. disconcerted, disappointed by reason of Jer 2:36 (twice in verse); Jer 12:13 ; Jer 48:13 ; Isa 1:29 ; Isa 20:5 ; Ezek 32:30 ; Ezek 36:32 . 3. with object בּשְׁתִּי לִשְׁאוֺל I am ashamed to ask Ezek 8:22 לֹא תֵבשׁוּ תַּהְכְּרוּ לִי ye are not ashamed to deal hardly with me (imperfect subject) Job 19:3 . בּושׁ often || נכלם & חפר ; בּשׁוּ וְהָכְלְמוּ they are ashamed and confounded Jer 14:3 ; Jer 22:22 Isa 2 , Isa 41:11 ; Isa 45:16 ; Isa 45:17 ; Ezek 16:52 ; Ezek 36:32 ; Ps 35:4 ; Ps 69:7 ; Ezek 9:6 וּבשׁוּ הַחֹזִים וְחָֽפְרוּ הַקֹּסְמִים and the seers shall be ashamed and the diviners confounded Mic 3:7 , compare Jer 15:9 ; Job 6:20 ; Ps 35:26 ; Ps 40:15 ; Ps 70:3 ; Ps 71:24 יֵבוֺשׁ מְקוֺרוֺ Hos 13:15 (read יִיבַשׁ be dry ); עַדבּֿוֺשׁ to the point of confusion Judg 3:25 (compare GFM), 2Kgs 2:17 ; 2Kgs 8:11 . Polel Perfect בּשֵׁשׁ delay (in shame), בּשֵׁשׁ משֶׁה לָרֶדֶת Moses delayed to descend Exod 32:1 ( J ), מַדּוּעַ בּשֵׁשׁ רִכְבּוֺ לָבוֺא why delay his chariots to come ? Judg 5:28 . Hiph`il 1. הֱבִישׁוֺתָ Ps 44:8 הֱבִישֹׁתָה Ps 53:6 Imperfect 2 masculine singular suffix תְּבִישֵׁנִי Ps 119:31 ; Ps 119:116 תָּבִישׁוּ Ps 14:6 put to shame, Participle מֵבִישׁ Prov 10:5 ; Prov 14:35 ; Prov 19:26 ; Prov 29:15 one causing shame or acting shamefully , || מִשְׂכִּיל ; עֶבֶד מַשְׂכִּיל יִמְשֹׁל בְּבֵן מֵבִישׁ a servant acting wisely will rule over a son causing shame Prov 17:2 מְבִישָׁה || אֵשֶׁת חַיִל Prov 12:4 . 2. הוֺבִישׁ 2Sam 19:6 ; Jer 2:26 ; Jer 6:15 ; Joel 1:10 ; Joel 1:12 הֹבִישׁ Jer 10:14 + 7 t., Hos 2:7 ; Joel 1:12 ; Joel 1:17 ; Isa 30:5 (but הבאיש Kt ); הֹבִשׁוּ Jer 8:9 ; Jer 8:12 Imperative הֹבִישׁוּ Joel 1:11 (all the forms in Joel derived √ יָבֵשׁ by ancient versions and some moderns, see Ew § 122 e Ges «GKC:72»§ 72 , 6). \\ \\ a. put to shame 2Sam 19:6 . \\ \\ b. act shamefully Hos 2:7 . \\ \\ c. to be put to shame Jer 2:26 ; Jer 6:15 ; Jer 46:24 ; Jer 48:1 (twice in verse); Jer 48:20 ; Jer 50:2 (twice in verse); Joel 1:10 ; Joel 1:12 ; Joel 1:17 (?). \\ \\ d. be ashamed Jer 8:9 ; Jer 8:12 ; Joel 1:11 ; Joel 1:12 (?) Isa 30:5 ( Qr ); with מִן Jer 10:14 = Jer 51:17 . Hithpa`el Imperfect יִתְבּשָׁ֑שׁוּ ashamed before one another Gen 2:25 ( J ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB980')\">BDB980</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H954')\">H954</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB979')\">BDB979</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB981')\">BDB981</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>בּוֺשׁ</bdbheb><sub>109</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be ashamed</highlightword> (Sabean <bdbheb>בוס</bdbheb>; <bdbheb>מהבאס</bdbheb> = <highlight>evil-doer</highlight> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('DHM')\">DHM<sup>ZMG 1883, 375, ||</sup></lookup> Aramaic <bdbarc>בְּהַת</bdbarc>, Syriac <placeholder538/>; Arabic <placeholder539/>, <placeholder540/> mean <highlight>disperse</highlight>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <ref ref=\"Jer 48:39\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"39\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"39\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,39)\">Jer 48:39</ref> <bdbheb>בּשׁ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 48:13\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(24